 "means": "every form appearing in a program this lane compiled with Apple's own compiler, checked against the width D2 admits for its opcode",
 "prefix_relationships": [],
 "the_mechanism": "the contract stores ONE `apple_witness` per opcode and D2 takes its width from that exemplar's byte count. An opcode Apple emits at more than one width is therefore admissible at one of them only, and which one is a property of the harvest rather than of the evidence. 38 of the 84 forms seen here fall outside D2 on that basis. Every one of them DOES have a structural record at the width it was emitted at, so the population a width-enumerating builder cannot reach is now empty; what remains is an admissibility gap, not a coverage hole.",
 "what_this_does_NOT_do": "it does not move anything into D2. The denominator's basis is published and cited by another lane; widening it from this side would leave two lanes quoting the same name for different populations. What is published here is the population and its evidence, so the decision is visible rather than made silently.",
 "what_would_make_this_WRONG": "if `g17ref.walk` assigned a different length to these bytes than the harvest does to the stored witness, the disagreement would be an instrument defect rather than a second width. The bytes are recorded for every form that has them, so the claim is checkable rather than asserted: an opcode whose local bytes are a PREFIX of the stored witness, or vice versa, would be the signature of that defect."
